  "question": {
    "text": "In a hydraulic lift, the surface area of the input piston is \\(6 \\mathrm{~cm}^2\\) and that of the output piston is \\(1500 \\mathrm{~cm}^2\\). If 100 N force is applied to the input piston to raise the output piston by 20 cm, then the work done is _______ kJ.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7vB0Nz4YRxMdUNSrjz-KO7V4bN7Up-BnJqPQ4PqEMp0.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\n\n\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{\\mathrm{F}_1}{\\mathrm{~A}_1}=\\frac{\\mathrm{F}_2}{\\mathrm{~A}_2}, \\frac{100}{6}=\\frac{\\mathrm{F}}{1500}, \\mathrm{~F}=\\frac{50}{3} \\times 1500 \\\\ & \\mathrm{~F}=50 \\times 500=25 \\times 10^3 \\mathrm{~N} \\\\ & \\omega=\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{F}} . \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{S}}=25 \\times 10^3 \\times \\frac{20}{100} \\\\ & =5 \\times 10^3=5 \\mathrm{~kJ}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
